<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mazouna</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mazouna is a small town in north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/algeria">Algeria</a>, in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dahra">Dahra</a> hills east of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oran">Oran</a>. From 1563 it was the first seat of the Ottoman <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beylik">Beylik</a> of the West, before the capital moved to Mascara around 1700. It was known as a centre of religious learning, with a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madrasa">madrasa</a> that trained scholars of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maliki-school">Maliki</a> law.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mazouna.jpg" alt="Mazouna" width="320" height="239" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Greatmazne · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mazouna.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
